@startuml cancel-shutdown-sequence
title M3a stop request, actual return and Host-owned disposal
actor User
participant Host
participant InspectionEngine as Engine
participant InspectionRunner as Runner
participant IInspector as Inspector
participant CancellationTokenSource as CTS
participant "Token callbacks" as Callbacks
participant "Timeout timer" as Timer
Runner -> Inspector : InspectAsync(job, samples, token)
User -> Engine : CancelRun(runId)
Engine -> Engine : first reason wins shared lock / CancelRequested
Engine -> CTS : CancelAsync()
CTS --> Engine : delivery task (token already canceled)
CTS ->> Callbacks : dispatch registered callbacks
Engine --> User : Accepted (still Busy)
note over Inspector, Callbacks
M2 native inspection is synchronous and returns on its own.
Token cancellation is not native stop completion.
end note
Inspector --> Runner : actual return (result or exception)
opt assessment returned
Runner -> Engine : persistence boundary if result returned
Engine --> Runner : reject persistence when stop already accepted
end
Runner --> Engine : actual runner return / error
Engine -> Engine : close completion arbitration
Engine -> CTS : await callback delivery
Callbacks --> CTS : callbacks finished
CTS --> Engine : complete (or callback error)
Engine -> Timer : await DisposeAsync()
Engine -> CTS : Dispose()
Engine -> Engine : finalize Canceled/TimedOut (or Faulted)
Engine -> Engine : release slot / complete handle
Engine --> Host : completed snapshot
Host -> Engine : await DisposeAsync()
Engine --> Host : Disposed
Host -> Inspector : Dispose owned adapter
note over Host, Engine
If Host disposes during a run: close new admission,
request Shutdown, then wait for the same completion.
Persisting rejects late stop requests and must finish saving.
Native Start/RequestStop/Wait and native callbacks arrive in M3b.
end note
@enduml
